      <name>Kerem es-Samra (Kerem el-Ajez) (כרם א-סמרא (כרם אל עג&apos;ז))</name>
      <description>A large pool measuring 22x18m, located in the southwest of the fortress, with collapsed walls. It served as a water reservoir for the Iron Age II fortress.&#10;&#10;Installation: Water Reservoir&#10;Era: 09. Iron Age II (-1000 to -586 BCE)&#10;Region: Judean Desert&#10;Precision: Exact Archaeological Site / IAA Grid&#10;Section: 2.9.30&#10;Pages: 167</description>
