    <Placemark>
      <name>Mezer (מצר)</name>
      <description>Multiple rock-cut cisterns, including a large one (B3) 5m deep and another (D7) with niches, were used for rainwater collection via rock-cut channels. These cisterns were unplastered due to the impermeable Nari and chalk bedrock.&#10;&#10;Installation: Deep Well&#10;Era: 05. Early Bronze Age (EB) (-3300 to -2200 BCE)&#10;Region: Coastal Plain&#10;Precision: Exact Archaeological Site / IAA Grid&#10;Section: 2.5.15&#10;Pages: 68</description>
