    <Placemark>
      <name>Khirbet Marjameh (חורבת מרג&apos;מה)</name>
      <description>A rock-cut cistern opening was found near the 8th-century BCE fortifications, though its size and plaster type are unknown. The primary water source for the city was the large Ein Samia spring nearby. Cisterns or pools were found at Qala&apos; Marjama, dated to the Iron Age II period.&#10;&#10;Installation: Plastered Cistern&#10;Era: 09. Iron Age II (-1000 to -586 BCE)&#10;Region: Samaria&#10;Precision: Exact Archaeological Site / IAA Grid&#10;Section: 2.9.22&#10;Pages: 162, 191</description>
