    <Placemark>
      <name>Horbat Radum (חורבת רדום)</name>
      <description>Two depressions, approximately 2m in diameter, were found outside the northern wall of this late Iron Age II fortress. These are identified as likely blocked cisterns that served the fortification. Cisterns or pools were found at Radum, dated to the Iron Age II period.&#10;&#10;Installation: Plastered Cistern&#10;Era: 09. Iron Age II (-1000 to -586 BCE)&#10;Region: Negev&#10;Precision: Exact Archaeological Site / IAA Grid&#10;Section: 2.9.35&#10;Pages: 170, 191</description>
