    <Placemark>
      <name>Tel Ashdod (תל אשדוד)</name>
      <description>A plastered pool (4162) measuring 3.2x1.5m, found in Area G within a governor&apos;s house or palace (Strata XIV-XVII, Late Bronze Age II). It had two phases, with a brick layer beneath the plaster floor, and a drainage channel leading to a stone-lined drainage pit. Water likely collected from roofs or was manually brought from a well.&#10;&#10;Installation: Water Reservoir&#10;Era: 07. Late Bronze Age (LB) (-1550 to -1200 BCE)&#10;Region: Coastal Plain&#10;Precision: Exact Archaeological Site / IAA Grid&#10;Section: 2.7.8&#10;Pages: 103, 104</description>
