    <Placemark>
      <name>Tel Gamma (תל ג&apos;מה)</name>
      <description>A sealed well, evidenced by large stones with rope marks and a depression that fills with water, located 400m southwest of Nahal Besor, at the foot of the acropolis. Possibly dates to the initial phase of the lower city in the Late Bronze Age.&#10;&#10;Installation: Deep Well&#10;Era: 07. Late Bronze Age (LB) (-1550 to -1200 BCE)&#10;Region: Negev&#10;Precision: Exact Archaeological Site / IAA Grid&#10;Section: 2.7.2&#10;Pages: 98</description>
